INT. SENTENCING HEARING, SMALL COURTROOM - DAY

A modest county courtroom, oak benches worn smooth by decades of hands. A flag in the corner, faded by afternoon light. A stenographer's keys click and then stop.

JUDGE CORNELIUS ABERNATHY-OKOYE (70s, a face like folded paper, half-moon glasses) looks down from the bench. Before him, standing at the defense table, a woman in a plain gray suit: SERAPHINA DUBOIS-TANAKA (40s, bookkeeper, wedding ring she keeps turning). Beside her, her ATTORNEY, MALCOLM ASHFORD-IGWE (50s, silvered temples), holds a single sheet of paper.

Across the aisle, the PROSECUTOR, ODALYS FERRARI-NKEMELU (30s, hair in a low knot), sits very straight.

ABERNATHY
Mr. Ashford-Igwe. You wished to be heard.

MALCOLM
I did, Your Honor.

ABERNATHY
Go ahead.

MALCOLM
(together)
My client has no prior record.

ODALYS ^
(together)
The State recommends the maximum.

Each hears the other. Malcolm stops. Odalys does not.

ODALYS (CONT'D)
She embezzled four hundred thousand dollars from a church fund.

MALCOLM
She repaid three hundred and ten.

ODALYS
After she was caught.

MALCOLM
Before she was charged.

ABERNATHY
Counsel, one at a time.

He lifts his glasses and rubs the bridge of his nose. Seraphina's thumb has gone still on her ring.

ABERNATHY (CONT'D)
Ms. Dubois-Tanaka. Is there something you wish to say?

SERAPHINA
No, sir.

ABERNATHY
You're allowed.

SERAPHINA
I know.

ABERNATHY
Then I'll ask again.

She glances at Malcolm, who gives the smallest nod. She lets go of her ring and rests both hands flat on the table.

SERAPHINA
My mother was ill. The church was kind, and I was careful, and then I wasn't.

ABERNATHY
Go on.

SERAPHINA
That's all of it, Your Honor.

Silence. The flag stirs in a draft from the air vent. Odalys looks at her own folded hands.

ABERNATHY
Ms. Ferrari-Nkemelu. Does the State wish to respond?

ODALYS
(a long beat)
No, Your Honor.

ABERNATHY
No?

ODALYS
The State withdraws its recommendation.

Malcolm looks at her sharply. She doesn't look back. Seraphina's shoulders drop an inch.

ABERNATHY
I'll take the matter under advisement.

He closes the folder. The gavel rises, hovers, comes down gently.

ABERNATHY (CONT'D)
We're adjourned.

He stands. The courtroom stirs. Seraphina stays where she is, gazing at the empty bench.
